{
  "_": "Starter pack seeded into the config on first install (config file absent + no backups). See config::build_starter_config. Every entry carries \"isStarter\": true so a future 'reset starter' or migration pass can identify seeded rows. Unassigned Library section is auto-expanded on first install via Sidebar.jsx's default-false state (no localStorage key yet). Pack C radial segments are INLINE GLOBAL::RADIAL:: assignments (independent copies of the same actions in Pack A) — the radial editor pane doesn't currently render the linked action from a Default::UNASSIGNED::-pointing segment, so inline keeps the editor UX working. Each Pack C segment carries a distinct lucide icon + colour so users can immediately see icons+colours are customisable. Expansion data.html fields carry the exact editor-DOM shape (rte-token spans + <br> line breaks) so RichTextEditor.innerHTML paint isn't blank; date/time tokens must use the whitelisted literal-string grammar in expansions.rs (e.g. `{date:D MMMM YYYY}`, `{time:HH:MM}` — NOT strftime like `{date:%H:%M}`). Pack F (starterPackVersion 2, 2026-09-02): two app-specific profiles, Excel (linkedApp EXCEL.EXE, Ctrl+Shift+letter) and Chrome (chrome.exe, Alt+letter), each with its own radial wheel whose segments REFERENCE the profile's own hotkey assignments (not inline copies). App profiles are Pro: they run during the first-install trial and go quiet on Free, which is the point (the trial-end modal reports fires inside Excel and Chrome). Match is on the lowercase process stem in foreground.rs, so a bare exe name is enough.",
  "starterPackVersion": 2,
  "profiles": [
    "Default",
    "Excel",
    "Chrome"
  ],
